s I-72 section)","captures":"on","compile_cost_definition":"eager-jit-adjacent (capability_set_v1.md 7.1/7.2): the explicit RegexBuilder::build() call, timed in-driver (`compile`). CAVEAT: like re2-default/re2-longest, this call does NOT build the runtime DFA -- the `regex` crate's lazy DFA is built INCREMENTALLY at match time and cached (N2 5). A reader pooling this testee beside pcre2-jit under one eager-jit table is comparing two different compile-cost SHAPES that happen to share a class token; the reporter's 7.2 footnote fires on exactly this definition-string mismatch. Median of N with spread is the REPORTER's reduction.","compile_phases":["compile"],"conventions":["perl-leftmost-first"],"engine_commit":null,"engine_metadata_declaration":{"named_count":{"description":"distinct named capture groups in the pattern (testees/onig/adapter.py's `names` pair, same shape)","scope":"pattern","source":"Regex::capture_names().filter(Option::is_some).count()","type":"integer"},"ncapturegroups":{"description":"lexical capturing groups in the pattern (the overall match, group 0, is not counted -- the same convention testees/re2/adapter.py and testees/onig/adapter.py already use)","scope":"pattern","source":"Regex::captures_len() - 1","type":"integer"},"refusal_class":{"description":"'size-limit' for CompiledTooBig (size_limit or dfa_size_limit exceeded); 'syntax' for every other named variant, incl. the structural 'invalid UTF-8 pattern' refusal this adapter raises itself before the regex crate ever sees the pattern (see the I-72 section, testees/rust/CLAUDE.md)","scope":"pattern","source":"the regex::Error variant name RegexBuilder::build() returned on a did-not-compile outcome, bucketed by this adapter (capability_set_v1.md 5.5: 'declared ONLY by a config whose engine gives a closed, structural signal' -- regex::Error's two named variants, Syntax and CompiledTooBig, are exactly that, and the type is #[non_exhaustive] so a third variant added upstream degrades to `syntax` r